title:: DragonFly Reverb Ports
summary:: SuperCollider ports of Michael Willis's Dragonfly Reverb plugins
categories:: UGens>Effects
related:: Classes/EarlyReflectionsDF, Classes/HallDF, Classes/PlateDF, Classes/RoomDF

description::

The DragonFlyReverb-SuperCollider-Port project provides four native SuperCollider UGens that wrap the DSP algorithms from Michael Willis's open-source Dragonfly Reverb plugin suite. Dragonfly Reverb is heavily based on algorithms from Freeverb3 (specifically the code::earlyref::, code::zrev2::, and code::progen:: models), offering high-quality lush reverbs for a variety of acoustic spaces.

This port vendors the C++ DSP core of Dragonfly Reverb directly into SuperCollider plugins, bypassing the need for a VST host or VSTPlugin while maintaining the same parameter scaling and sound character.

subsection:: UGens

The following four UGens are provided:

list::
## link::Classes/EarlyReflectionsDF:: - Dragonfly Early Reflections. Uses the Freeverb3 code::earlyref:: model to simulate the first few reflections of a room, providing spatial cues without a long reverberant tail.
## link::Classes/HallDF:: - Dragonfly Hall Reverb. Combines the code::earlyref:: model with the code::zrev2:: late-reverb model to simulate large, dense acoustic spaces like concert halls.
## link::Classes/PlateDF:: - Dragonfly Plate Reverb. Uses a modified Freeverb3 model to simulate the bright, metallic density of a physical plate reverberator.
## link::Classes/RoomDF:: - Dragonfly Room Reverb. Combines the code::earlyref:: model with a scaled-down late-reverb model optimized for smaller, more intimate acoustic spaces.
::

